<p>U.S. Central Command said American forces fired on the Iranian-flagged oil tanker M/T Hasna in the Gulf of Oman on Wednesday, disabling it as it tried to sail toward an Iranian port in violation of a U.S. blockade. The strike occurred as President Trump pressed Tehran to accept a proposed deal to end a two-month war and issued a fresh public ultimatum. Reports described movement toward a possible agreement, but Tehran’s response to Washington’s latest plan remained unclear.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/COUzXJWgcpRccLI9OmfBkwF3KLnDe-I3GdWgAbalG9UlJ0u0Ib4Xs2rVbNLKb3RQzIH-ix0T_kI-7OTz1PZRta-OYFQVntXEgcvUn1PFlA' alt='An Iranian tugboat in the Strait of Hormuz off Bandar Abbas.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Ceasefire context: The Korea Times reported the attack occurred while Iran and the United States were officially in a ceasefire and as both sides appeared to be moving closer to an initial agreement.</li><li>Reported deal terms: Aaj TV said the proposed settlement reportedly went beyond shipping to include halting uranium enrichment, lifting sanctions and releasing frozen funds.</li></ul><blockquote>If they don’t agree, the bombing starts, and it will be, sadly, at a much higher level and intensity than it was before - President Donald Trump</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>U.S. Central Command: CENTCOM said the U.S. blockade remained in full effect for vessels seeking to enter or leave Iranian ports, even after President Trump paused Project Freedom. (<a href='https://www.defensenews.com/news/your-navy/2026/05/06/us-forces-fire-at-disable-iran-flagged-tanker-trying-to-evade-blockade/'>Defense News</a>)</li><li>President Donald Trump: Trump said Iran’s acceptance of what he described as already-agreed terms would end Epic Fury and allow the blockade to open the Hormuz Strait to all traffic, including Iran. (<a href='https://www.koaa.com/us-news/iran-war/trump-issues-bombing-starts-ultimatum-in-strait-of-hormuz-dispute'>KOAA</a>)</li><li>Ir